    "explanation": "Both parties' accounts point the same way, and the record decides the case.\n\nMeasuring the trip. The fare is metered (EV-FARE-00102, fare_model METERED), so the route-deviation rules apply. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH establishment tests to pass: an excess greater than 0.8 km AND greater than 20% of the optimal distance. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00102) is unbroken — 193 fixes, 10-second sampling against a 10-second expected interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, largest gap 0 seconds — and it measures 21.79 km over the trace polyline (the governing field; the trip record's rounded 21.8 km convenience copy may not be cited for the test). The platform's optimal distance is 20.4 km (EV-TRIP-00102). The excess is therefore 1.39 km, which is 6.81% of 20.4 km. It clears the absolute limb (1.39 km > 0.8 km) but fails the proportional limb (6.81%, well short of 20%). Both tests must pass, so no route deviation is established. The metered fare of SGD 29.91 that the rider paid stands; no part of the SGD 7.00 she contested is returned, and payment_status CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00 is left as it is. POL-RD-02 does not run: its recomputation (which would give 27.46 and a 2.45 difference) applies only once a deviation is established, and none is. Both advocates read the arithmetic to the same conclusion and every claim on this point is accepted.\n\nWhy the driver's traffic excuse neither helps nor escalates. The driver's explanation — a slow crawl on the BKE near Dairy Farm — is an asserted external traffic cause, tested under POL-RD-13 against a traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else. The only advisory artifact in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-00102-01, is MISSING: weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, no payload, no coverage of the BKE or the Upper Bukit Timah corridor in the 11:16–11:55 window. The comparison POL-RD-03 requires cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. It does not excuse anything — but nothing needs excusing, because the threshold already fails on the rider's own evidence. Because the driver named no advisory evidence ID, the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle, not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged.\n\nRider-requested detour. The only in-app message on this trip is the driver's own (EV-CHAT-00102, 'boss BKE quite jam, i go Upper Bukit Timah ok?', sent 11:29:04, read 11:29:40, never answered). It is not a rider instruction, carries waypoint_hint null and names no road with the specificity POL-RD-04 demands, so POL-RD-04 excludes nothing on the driver's behalf. No distance is excluded and no compensation arises: the rider was billed for 21.8 km against a trace of 21.79 km, so there is no unbilled-distance shortfall to pay under POL-RD-04's compensation limb.\n\nBilling integrity. EV-FARE-00102 itemises no ERP or toll gantry lines (erp_gantries empty, tolls_erp 0.00, on- and off-optimal-route ERP totals 0.00) and no airport surcharge on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport. Base fare 3.80, distance 16.35, time 8.96 and platform fee 0.80 reconcile to the metered rate card against the 29.91 charged. There is no phantom charge to refund under POL-RD-09(4), so no billing-integrity referral fires. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes, so POL-RD-07's corroboration requirement and POL-RD-10(3) are not in play, and none of the POL-RD-06 driver-profile conditions is met (deviation_flags_90d 0), so no conduct referral fires either.\n\nThe precedents sharing these clauses (P-0001, P-0002) ended in partial refunds because their excess met the POL-RD-01 threshold; here the 6.81% proportional limb fails, and that is what makes the difference. The monetary effect is nil, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, and this ruling is provisional — either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
